# OS / editor junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# Convention: anything kept local-only goes in private/
private/

# Secrets — NEVER commit AWS or model-provider credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
.aws/
credentials

# Terraform — state holds resource IDs and can hold secrets in plaintext
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
.terraform/
crash.log
crash.*.log
# NOTE: .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored. It pins provider versions and hashes and
# belongs in version control, exactly like uv.lock. Ignoring it makes provider versions
# non-reproducible between machines and CI.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Node / frontend
node_modules/
.next/
.vite/

# Local data artifacts — the ingestion output lives in S3 and is rebuilt from source.
# data/ is fully untracked, which also keeps it off the GitHub root listing. The tracked pointer to
# the pinned artifact version gets a home in the v0.1 IMPLEMENTATION doc; it is not this directory.
data/
*.parquet
*.sqlite3

# Eval run output in `eval/results/` is ALL COMMITTED as of 2026-09-10, phase 7.5 step 1. Decided by
# sjtroxel. Nothing here ignores it any more, and that is deliberate.
#
# History, because the reasoning is the point. From phase 4 the directory was ignored as "reproducible by
# re-running the suite", with exceptions negated back in: `-judge.json` (2026-08-20 — "a number quoted in
# a doc whose evidence lives on one laptop does not satisfy that"), then `-tier2.json` and `-heldout.json`
# (2026-08-24). Plain `-bedrock.json` runs stayed ignored because "re-running one answers the same question
# again". That holds for a BENCHMARK and fails for a HISTORY: a re-run answers the same question with
# different numbers — the noise floor exists because it does — and the live gate bounds, the published
# report and the trend view all cite runs that cannot be re-created. The five 2026-09-07 baseline runs
# ($2.61, ~2.4 hours) were living on one laptop, which is the judge-file argument exactly.
#
# Size was never the issue: 29 files, 452 KB at the change, ~15 KB per run after it, and no account ids,
# keys or held-out content in them (checked). Smoke tests, subset runs and the aborted run are committed
# too — choosing which runs to keep would be curating the record, and `eval/thresholds.py` already refuses
# to join incomparable runs.
eval-results/

# AWS SAM / build litter
.aws-sam/

# TypeScript incremental build state (web/). Regenerated by `tsc -b`.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Phase 5 design previews (steps 3, 5, 6, 7). Throwaway by construction, per the phase 5
# IMPLEMENTATION doc 6 — they exist to be looked at once and then deleted. What survives is the
# DECISION, recorded in that doc's 12. Keeping the previews would invite maintaining them.
web/previews/

# The graph artifact staged into the SPA by `web/scripts/stage-graph.mjs`. Generated, 2.6 MB at
# artifact v0.7.1, and a byte-for-byte copy of the pinned artifact already in git. Regenerated by
# `npm run build` via the `prebuild` hook, which is why re-pinning the SPA costs no repository bytes.
web/public/graph/
